            <report>
                <DQ_AbsoluteExternalPositionalAccuracy>
                    <measureDescription>
                        <gco:CharacterString>The Polygon Accuracy measure is intended to ensure that statistical area polygons are accurate.</gco:CharacterString>
                    </measureDescription>
                    <evaluationMethodDescription>
                        <gco:CharacterString>Regulatory coordinates (e.g., Registration Areas, Districts, Subdistricts) were recorded from the 2015 - 2016 Alaska Fish and Game Laws and Regulations, and plotted over the groundfish statistical area feature class (PVG_Statewide_2001). Statitical area boundaries that follow regualtory boundaries were aligned to regulatory coordinates. All polygons were examined for accuracy by regional staff (Regional Supervisors, Fishery Coordinators, Biologists, Regional GIS Representatives). Specific coordinates and regualtory authority can be found on the ADF&amp;G Commercial Fisheries Available Statistical Area Coordinates confluence page (https://www.admin.adfg.state.ak.us/confluence/pages/viewpage.action?pageId=63897806).</gco:CharacterString>
                    </evaluationMethodDescription>
                    <result gco:nilReason="missing"/>
                </DQ_AbsoluteExternalPositionalAccuracy>
            </report>
            <lineage>
                <LI_Lineage>
                    <processStep>
                        <LI_ProcessStep>
                            <description>
                                <gco:CharacterString>The original statistical area lines were converted from a shape file to an Arc/Info coverage. Then each line in this coverage was coded based on its type (e.g. coastline, 3-nautical-mile-line, statistical area grid line, land-based point-to-point statistical area line, and fixed regulatory line). (T. Haverland)</gco:CharacterString>
                            </description>
                            <dateTime>
                                <gco:DateTime>2000-02-09T00:00:00</gco:DateTime>
                            </dateTime>
                        </LI_ProcessStep>
                    </processStep>
                    <processStep>
                        <LI_ProcessStep>
                            <description>
                                <gco:CharacterString>Lines were converted from NAD27 to NAD83. Some of the lines in this coverage were based on hard lines of latitude or longitude (statistical area grid lines and regulatory lines), therefore the coverage could not be converted to NAD83 as a whole. The statistical area grid lines and regulatory lines had to be separated from the other line types and defined as referenced to the NAD83 datum with no conversion. The remaining lines were converted to NAD83 using Arc/Info's PROJECT command, and all line types were appended into one coverage (gnd14ap). Then this coverage was edited to fix dangles, overshoots, missing or incorrect arcs, and other line topological errors. (T. Haverland)</gco:CharacterString>
                            </description>
                            <dateTime>
                                <gco:DateTime>2000-09-15T00:00:00</gco:DateTime>
                            </dateTime>
                        </LI_ProcessStep>
                    </processStep>
                    <processStep>
                        <LI_ProcessStep>
                            <description>
                                <gco:CharacterString>Polygon centroids were added to the line coverage gnd29ed from pvg_stat. Polygon topology was built and the coverage was edited. (T. Haverland)</gco:CharacterString>
                            </description>
                            <dateTime>
                                <gco:DateTime>2000-09-26T00:00:00</gco:DateTime>
                            </dateTime>
                        </LI_ProcessStep>
                    </processStep>
                    <processStep>
                        <LI_ProcessStep>
                            <description>
                                <gco:CharacterString>Projected coverage to geographic and created shapefile. Merged shapefile with pvsstat1 and pvsdist1 so that shapefile contained all valid groundfish and shellfish statistical areas plus district-wide statistical areas for Southeast Alaska (these statistical areas (e.g. 010100) were used historically to record groundfish and shellfish catch when only the district was known. Added attributes to shapefile and populated using values from pvg_stat and from a spreadsheet created by G. Smith. Edited attributes. Created final shapefiles pvg_stat_2001 and pvi_stat_2001 so that each shapefile contains all current valid statistical areas for the groundfish and shellfish fisheries respectively. (T. Haverland)</gco:CharacterString>
                            </description>
                            <dateTime>
                                <gco:DateTime>2000-11-22T00:00:00</gco:DateTime>
                            </dateTime>
                        </LI_ProcessStep>
                    </processStep>
                    <processStep>
                        <LI_ProcessStep>
                            <description>
                                <gco:CharacterString>Polygons were split to create new statistical areas. In some cases, the new lines were digitized by the area offices and sent to ADF&amp;G CF HQ as a MapInfo table or ArcView shape files. In others, the changes were based on coordinates in ADF&amp;G and Federal regulations. The old statistical area numbers were retired and new numbers assigned. (T. Haverland)</gco:CharacterString>
                            </description>
                            <dateTime>
                                <gco:DateTime>2000-11-22T00:00:00</gco:DateTime>
                            </dateTime>
                        </LI_ProcessStep>
                    </processStep>
                    <processStep>
                        <LI_ProcessStep>
                            <description>
                                <gco:CharacterString>Coastal statistical area polygons were clipped to the 1: 63,360 resolution shoreline published by the Alaska Department of Natural Resources (1998-02-11) (L. Hulbert and S. Larsen)</gco:CharacterString>
                            </description>
                            <dateTime>
                                <gco:DateTime>2016-10-11T00:00:00</gco:DateTime>
                            </dateTime>
                        </LI_ProcessStep>
                    </processStep>
                    <processStep>
                        <LI_ProcessStep>
                            <description>
                                <gco:CharacterString>Simplified the geometry of polygons. Many polygons contained multiple verteces that did not alter the overall line shape. These vertexes were individually examined, and deleted on a case by case basis. (S. Larsen)</gco:CharacterString>
                            </description>
                            <dateTime>
